    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2532,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5026,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "This is likely a good decision. Our current polls suggest that Brexit is our strongest issue."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2533,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5027,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "With the terrorist attacks in France over the last couple of years, this might not be a bad idea. Many are concerned about their safety from similar attacks potentially happening at home."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2534,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5028,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "You unveil your manifesto in Kilburn to a somewhat apathetic crowd of Londoners, ending without much fanfare or interest, which contrasts with Jeremy Corbyn’s much more explosive start out of the Labour manifesto unveiling."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2535,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5029,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "To an audience of roughly 100, mostly made up by students and academics, you release a manifesto that got a few paying attention, a little bit of interest that paled in comparison to Corbyn’s manifesto unveiling."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2536,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5031,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "You head up to Giffnock in East Renfrewshire and you deliver a rather uninspired unveiling of your manifesto. You ended up quickly taking a backseat to Ruth Davidson who managed to inspire a little enthusiasm for the Scottish Conservative cause, which contrasts with a very enthusiastic Corbyn manifesto unveiling."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2537,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5000,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "Alright, time to end Parliamentary gridlock, and this is a great message to start on in the face of such an unpopular opponent."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2538,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5034,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "We’re not so sure. We don’t think this is something you can just dance around, it will come back to bite you in the debates."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2544,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5033,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "We understand your need to get back campaigning again as soon as possible, so we’ll give some brief lessons to hopefully iron out the biggest flaws in your communication ability. "
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2545,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5035,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "You will have a light schedule for the next week as we work to help you overcome these issues in your campaign."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2546,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5036,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "Of course this would come back to bite us, but giving a short gesture towards party unity and getting the conversation back to Brexit might be the best way you can handle it."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2547,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5037,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "Leaning into this very unpopular policy among the public will not help your campaign. At least Jacob Rees-Mogg is happy though."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2548,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5040,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "It’s appreciated that you’re trying to reduce the temperature after such a shocking act of inhumanity."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2552,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5041,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "As you visit Manchester, you end up meeting Jeremy Corbyn who is shaking hands with the family members of victims. You also meet up with them and connect on a personal level. The news broadcasts a heartwarming scene of both party leaders putting politics aside in the face of tragedy."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2553,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5042,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "Many nod along with these ideas, but they aren’t without controversy. Young people are concerned about the ideas of internet surveillance."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2554,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5043,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "It’s difficult to consider what should be said after an attack like this to minimise future harm. A horrible attack is likely to result in a horrible backlash, and many British Muslims appreciate that you haven’t roped them into this, although UKIP call the Conservatives weak on terrorism, like clockwork."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2555,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5044,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "You can’t say that austerity has failed publicly, but some subtle proposals to reverse some of the most severe cuts might play well in this political climate. Police funding is an area that even the most fiscal conservative partisans can’t attack without coming off as unreasonable."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2556,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5045,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "What is national security but just another Brexit issue? Brexit, Brexit, Brexit. That’s your strength, so trying to wrestle control of the national conversation in this way might be a good approach."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2561,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5046,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "It’s rich that Jeremy Corbyn is trying to hang the issue of national security over the heads of the Conservatives, but it’s frustrating that this is being rather successful against us. Perhaps reminding people of who Jeremy Corbyn is will get them to see sense once again?"
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2562,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5047,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "Bring it back to square 1. You’re already on the process to addressing these concerns. This election pivots on Brexit. In the end, who do you want leading the country into Donald Tusk’s negotiation room? Get the voters to think about that."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2563,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5048,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "With the recent hype of the national security issue, making an argument for a Hard Brexit with the appearance of an argument about national security might make the Hard Brexit medicine go down better."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2564,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5049,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "You are clarifying a preference for a Soft Brexit. This will help with moderates and Remain voters, it will likely be popular in Scotland, but you might struggle to pull UKIP’s votes towards the Conservatives if you make your Brexit stance too “soft”."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2568,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5050,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "The “no-deal” option sends shivers down the spines of Remainers, many of which are looking to desert the Conservative ship any way they can, but this strength is perceived with much more positivity in the Red Wall."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2569,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5051,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "Ruling out the no-deal option pacifies many Remainers, but it’s not like you’ve given a Soft Brexit position here. This very much still expresses issues like border security. In essence, it’s as big a tent as you can make the Brexit issue. Many are content, but not many are enthusiastic."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2570,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5052,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "That’s all they wanted to hear. “Brexit means Brexit”, music to the UKIP supporters’ ears."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2571,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5053,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "Many UKIP voters concern themselves heavily with immigration, and this idea of a “points-based” system has been picking up steam on the political right. This should win over a decent amount of UKIP’s support."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2572,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5054,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "Leaning in on the no-deal idea will certainly win over a lot of UKIP voters, but also it will alienate a lot of Remain voters from the Conservative camp. "
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2573,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5055,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "The “UKIP question” is a difficult one to answer, because it’s possible that under their less popular leader this time around, many will just come home to the Conservatives regardless, and at the same time, you don’t want to alienate other factions of voters from places like Scotland and the Home Counties."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2574,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5056,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "It’s always good to get across policy positions in interviews like this, but dear god did you come across as more wooden than a stool in this interview."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2587,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5057,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "One part of this interview ended up becoming a bit of a meme, when you talked about your bookish upbringing, and your worst childhood mischief involving you running through fields of wheat. Jeremy Corbyn soon made a joke about your “terrible behaviour”"
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2588,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5058,
            "candidate": 200,
            "answer_feedback": "This probably wasn’t your best approach, as you just end up playing into Corbyn’s strategy with trying to redirect the conversation. Perhaps this is a gamble on that it’s already changed, and you’re adapting your campaign?"
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback",
        "pk": 2589,
        "fields": {
            "answer": 5059,
            "candidate": 200,
